WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.103
-The president is resisting
calls to release his tax returns

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.439
and calling the people
who investigate him traitors.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.441
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.942
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:13.112 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.447
-Before we get to Trump,

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.916
a bunch of other crazy stuff
happened today.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.817
For example, you might remember
Michael Avenatti,

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:20.820
the guy who used to be
Stormy Daniels' lawyer.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.257
Well, today, Avenatti was
charged with 36 counts of fraud,

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.825
perjury, failure to pay taxes,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360
embezzlement, and other
financial crimes.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.095
And 36 counts is a lot.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.097
But when you look at him,
you think,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.799
"I thought it would have
been higher."

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.469
And the details of the
indictment are truly insane.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.671
"The L.A. Times" reports that
Avenatti stole

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.673
millions of dollars
from five clients.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.276
He put $2.5 million
of that money

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.144
into the purchase
of a private jet.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.613
And in the other case, the money
landed in the accounts

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.815
of GB Autosport, LLC,

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.786
which managed Avenatti's
racecar team.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.921
How is this the first
we're hearing

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:58.057
of Michael Avenatti's
racecar team?

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:01.460
That's the dead giveaway
that someone is bad news.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.998
The racecar track is where James
Bond meets the villain

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.132
for the first time as he's
pulling off his helmet

00:01:07.132 --> 00:01:08.534
and his racing gloves.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.568
[ As Bond villain ] Mr. Bond,

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.371
should we speak
somewhere quieter?

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.705
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.240
[ Normal voice ] Also,
did you not see "Goodfellas"?

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.341
When you rip people off,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.576
you gotta play it cool
with the money.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.911
You're like a guy
who buys a Ferrari

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.179
and asks for the vanity plate --
"Bank Robber."

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.348
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.817
While he was doing this,
Avenatti was actively

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.686
putting himself
in the spotlight.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.855
He said he was going to run
for President in 2020.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.958
He made more appearances on CNN
than the words "Breaking News."

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.661
And a lot of people
fell for Avenatti,

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.595
probably because his job
description was always

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:39.332
"attorney" and not
"racecar team owner!"

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.103
While that was happening,
WikiLeaks founder Julian Assange

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.471
was also arrested in London,

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.773
where he was dragged out
of the Ecuadorian embassy

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:50.143
looking like Santa Claus
with a manifesto.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.311
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.713
"You're all naughty!
I have it on my list!"

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.648
[ Applause ]

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.883
I mean...

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:00.219
Based on that treatment,
I can't wait to read

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.356
what Assange writes on the
Ecuador embassy's Airbnb page.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.824
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:08.627
Now Ecuador had granted Assange
asylum in their embassy,

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:11.363
but withdrew it, which allowed
U.K. authorities to arrest him.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.266
According to The Daily Beast,
Ecuador imposed a new

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.968
and detailed set of rules
on its fugitive guest,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.204
banning unannounced visitors
and requiring Assange

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.472
to pay his own medical bills,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.240
clean up after himself
in the bathroom,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.309
and tend to the well-being,
food, cleanliness,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.977
and proper care of his cat.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.113
Assange bristled
at the restrictions,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.315
and took Ecuador's foreign
ministry to court.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.651
He took them to court
over his cat.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.451
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:33.753
Usually people go to court

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.589
to get restraining orders
against their cats.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.224
"Please, your honor,
he keeps glaring at me

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.359
like he wants to kill me."

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.696
Now look, you can think Assange
is a creep, which he is,

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.532
and also be worried about what
this means for press freedom.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.600
But one person who's always been
very clear

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.702
about where he stands on
WikiLeaks is Donald Trump.

00:02:50.702 --> 00:02:52.939
And yet, when Trump was asked
today about WikiLeaks,

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.207
which he repeatedly praised
throughout the campaign,

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:57.209
he pretended he didn't know
anything about it.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:00.379
-Mr. president, do you
still love WikiLeaks?

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:03.582
-I know nothing about WikiLeaks.
It's not my thing.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:06.585
-Oh, it's not your thing?

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.621
Well, what is your thing?

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.390
-Who do you like in the Masters?
Who do you think will win?

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.026
-You know, there are 15 players
capable of winning,

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.895
and I guess you could say there
are a lot more than that.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.631
They're great players. I don't
think a field for the Masters

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.232
has ever been this deep.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:23.002
I was watching late last night,

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.037
and they were going over
the different players.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.607
I think the field
has never been so deep.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:33.078
But always Phil and Tiger
and...Dustin.

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:35.514
I mean, you have
so many great players.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:39.285
But they were just saying,
they're younger,

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.820
they're stronger, they have
never hit the ball this long.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.923
They have never hit the ball
this accurately.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.058
They have never putted better
than they do now.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.194
You know, the whole thing
is pretty incredible.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.029
But the field is very,
very deep.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.197
I think it's going to be
a great Masters.

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:54.801
-That's the most coherent answer
he's ever given.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.202
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.070
And it wasn't even
that coherent.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:02.274
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:05.678
If being President was just
answering golf questions,

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.780
this guy would be George
Washington.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.215
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.750
But seriously, how can you say
WikiLeaks is not your thing?

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.853
Your government just arrested
a guy whose organization

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.888
you repeatedly praised
throughout the campaign,

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.056
and you're acting like someone

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.658
just offered you weed
at a party.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.460
[ As Trump ] "Oh, no thanks,
man. That's not my thing."

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.694
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.596
[ Normal voice ]
Also, do you not remember

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.964
when you said all of this stuff?

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.233
-The sad part is we don't talk
about WikiLeaks.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.401
Because it's incredible.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.236
You see so much from
these WikiLeaks.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.237
You see so much.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.171
Boy, I love reading
those WikiLeaks.

00:04:33.171 --> 00:04:35.808
I'll tell you, this WikiLeaks
stuff is unbelievable.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.277
This WikiLeaks is like
a treasure trove.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.679
WikiLeaks is amazing.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.814
WikiLeaks! I love WikiLeaks.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.915
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.884
-[ As Trump ] I love WikiLeaks.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.951
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Normal voice ] He said it --

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.323
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:54.326
He said it like the guy
at the end of a rom-com

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.996
who can finally admit he's
in love with his best friend.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.532
"I can finally say it,
I love Carol!"

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.666
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.234
While Trump was dodging
questions about

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.703
his previous support
for WikiLeaks,

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.371
he was also dodging questions
about everything

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.039
from the Mueller Report
to his tax returns.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.775
Last week, Democrats requested

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:11.410
six years of Trump's personal
and business tax information

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.080
from 2013 to 2018,
including individual tax returns

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.183
and returns from eight
businesses linked to Trump --

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.684
eight businesses.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.519
Of course, it's hard to find
those returns

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:23.890
since seven of those businesses
went bankrupt years ago.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.058
if you want to find the tax
returns for Trump Steaks

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.427
or Trump Vodka, you have to go
deep into the IRS basement

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.930
and look in the box labeled
"obvious scams."

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.264
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:33.433
But the law is clear.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.535
Democrats on the house
Ways and Means Committee

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.703
have the power to request
Trump's tax returns.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.672
And yet Trump told reporters
yesterday

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.773
he would just flat out ignore
the request

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:44.943
using the same obviously false
excuse he's been using

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:48.047
since 2016 -- he's under audit.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.682
And towards the end
of his rambling answer,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.618
he found a way to start bragging
about his businesses.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.421
-While I'm under audit,
I won't do it.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.089
If I'm not under audit,
I would do it.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:58.423
I had no problem with it.

00:05:58.423 --> 00:06:01.026
But while I'm under audit,
I would not give my taxes.

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:03.095
There's no law whatsoever.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.265
Now, I will say this --

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.401
I would love to give them,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:11.470
but I'm not going to do it
while I'm under audit.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.440
What I have done is
approximately

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.877
a 104-page summary,

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:21.714
and really in great detail,
of assets and values

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:25.450
and -- Nobody wants to go over
that because it's so good.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.421
I built a great company,
one of the best companies.

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.823
I have some of the greatest
assets in the world.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.324
I did a good job.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:35.194
-Well, now he's just doing
affirmations in public.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.094
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.094 --> 00:06:37.296
[ As Trump ] "I did a good job.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:41.734
I'm good at business.
My wife does like me."

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.202
[ Normal voice ] Also,
can you please just drop

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.503
this dumb audit excuse?

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:47.039
It's obviously fake. You've been
saying it since 2016.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.641
There's no way it's taking
the IRS three years

00:06:49.641 --> 00:06:50.977
to go through your tax returns.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:53.512
And if it has, that doesn't
make you look great.

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:56.649
If you told someone it took you
a week to clean your kitchen,

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:59.452
they'd be like, "How [bleep] up
was your kitchen?"

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:01.387
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:05.824
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:10.930
While Trump is just ignoring
the law on his tax returns,

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.798
he's also sounding increasingly
unhinged

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:13.866
on the Russia investigation.

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.634
Now because Trump keeps lying
about it,

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.336
we have to just take
a step back here

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:20.873
and remember how all of this
got started.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.241
Russia hacked
the Democrats' e-mails

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.942
while they were doing
business deals with Trump

00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:25.711
and making contact with
Trump campaign officials.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.379
And the entire time these people
were lying about it.

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:28.915
And then when the FBI started
investigating it,

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:30.249
Trump asked the director
to shut it down

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.250
and pledge his loyalty to Trump.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.518
And when he refused,
Trump fired him.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.719
And then he said on TV
he fired him

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:34.954
because of the Russia
investigation.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:35.955
He told the Russians
he fired him

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.423
because of
the Russia investigation.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:39.224
And then because his Republican
Attorney General had recused

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:41.627
himself, his Republican Deputy
Attorney General appointed

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:42.861
a special counsel, Robert
Mueller,

00:07:42.861 --> 00:07:45.364
who is a registered Republican.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.966
And, while this was happening,

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.600
Putin also gave Trump
a soccer ball.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.703
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:51.703 --> 00:07:54.306
Which was definitely,

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:56.709
definitely the first time Trump
ever saw a soccer ball.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:57.943
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.512
[ As Trump ] Thank you for
this beautiful gift.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:02.381
I'm going to say
a Russian bowling ball?

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.016
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.618
And it probably has,
when you open it,

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.920
a littler bowling ball in it?

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.855
And then another little one
and a then little one?

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:10.689
[ Applause ]

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.092
And hopefully at the end,

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.894
a tiny marshmallow?

00:08:15.894 --> 00:08:17.597
[ Normal voice ] I wish
I didn't have to keep recapping

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.131
all this stuff every time
we talk about it.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.399
I'm starting to think we're
just gonna need

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.868
a permanent scroll that stays up
throughout the show.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.036
But I have to keep recapping it

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:25.438
because Trump keeps
lying about it.

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:27.172
Yesterday, his Attorney General
repeated

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:29.541
Trump's conspiracy theory that
his campaign was spied on.

00:08:29.541 --> 00:08:31.544
And then Trump suggested
the investigation

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:33.312
was somehow illegal
or unwarranted,

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:36.215
and even said the people
investigating him were traitors.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:38.750
-It was an illegal
investigation.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.853
It was started illegally.

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.155
Everything about it was crooked,

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:46.424
every single thing about it.

00:08:46.424 --> 00:08:48.193
There were dirty cops.

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:50.062
These were bad people.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:53.331
And this was an attempted coup.

00:08:53.331 --> 00:08:56.001
This was an attempted takedown
of a president.

00:08:56.001 --> 00:08:59.672
This was an illegal witch hunt,
and everybody knew it.

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.107
And they knew it, too.
And they got caught.

00:09:02.107 --> 00:09:04.509
And what they did was treason.

00:09:04.509 --> 00:09:06.511
-My God, man.
Now you're accusing people

00:09:06.511 --> 00:09:07.947
of coups and treason.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:09.915
I'd say you should start
growing a dictator beard,

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.283
but based on your actual hair,

00:09:11.283 --> 00:09:12.951
I'm not sure how
that would look.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:15.854
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:19.091
This is why it's crucial
that decisions

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:21.560
involving the Mueller report
remain independent of Trump.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.929
And yet yesterday, when his
Attorney General William Barr

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:25.364
was asked if he briefed
the White House

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:27.800
on the Mueller report,
Barr's answer was very evasive.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.302
-Has anyone in the White House
seen any of the report?

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:32.505
-You know, I'm not gonna --
I'm not gonna -- as I said,

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:34.240
I'm landing the plane right now.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.576
And, uh, you know, I've been
willing to discuss my --

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:41.680
my letters and the process
going forward.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.217
But the report is going to be
out next week.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.319
And I'm just not going to get
into the details

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:49.755
of the process until
the plane is on the ground.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.690
-The plane has been
on the ground.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.559
Mueller landed the plane.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:57.129
You're the crew guy refusing
to drive the little gate thingy

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:58.264
up to the door...

00:09:58.264 --> 00:09:59.131
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:01.333
...so we can get off the plane.

00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:05.737
This is why --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:05.737 --> 00:10:08.407
This is why we need
aggressive oversight

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:09.775
of the Trump administration,

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:12.111
whether it's on the Mueller
report or his tax returns.

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:13.579
And yet Republicans
are doing the opposite.

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:14.880
They are protecting him.
For example,

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.348
after the Democratic chairman

00:10:16.348 --> 00:10:18.450
of the house Ways and Means
Committee, Richard Neal,

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.353
submitted his formal request to
the IRS for Trump's tax returns,

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:24.289
Louisiana Senator John Kennedy
went on TV and straight up

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.058
called Neal a moron.

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:31.696
-Chairman Neal, powerful man,
head of Ways and Means.

00:10:31.696 --> 00:10:34.833
I know he's an adult,

00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:37.036
but I don't think he's
like a real adult.

00:10:37.036 --> 00:10:38.304
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:41.506
He says that he needs
Trump's tax returns.

00:10:41.506 --> 00:10:44.844
He says it's policy,
not politics.

00:10:44.844 --> 00:10:47.312
He has said, I think on CNN,

00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:50.216
that the reason he needs them

00:10:50.216 --> 00:10:53.551
is that he needs to determine
how well the IRS

00:10:53.551 --> 00:10:56.288
is auditing taxpayers.

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:59.791
I can't believe he really thinks

00:10:59.791 --> 00:11:02.795
the American people
are gonna fall for that.

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:06.165
It must really suck
to be that dumb.

00:11:06.165 --> 00:11:08.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:10.335
-It doesn't suck to be
that dumb.

00:11:10.335 --> 00:11:12.070
It sucks for your boss
to be that dumb.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.773
That's the guy you answer to.

00:11:13.773 --> 00:11:15.841
Maybe think about
where your life is at.

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:17.143
You're a United States Senator,

00:11:17.143 --> 00:11:18.710
and you take marching orders
from a guy who

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.413
once got on Air Force One with
toilet paper stuck to his shoe.

00:11:21.413 --> 00:11:23.281
[ Laughter ]

00:11:23.281 --> 00:11:25.351
Republicans in Congress
keep trying to defend Trump

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:28.153
from Democrats, but their
efforts keep falling flat.

00:11:28.153 --> 00:11:30.489
And the dumbest example of that
came this week

00:11:30.489 --> 00:11:32.624
during a hearing
on Trump's climate policies.

00:11:32.624 --> 00:11:35.160
Democrats called former
Secretary of State John Kerry

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.762
as a witness,
and during the hearing,

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:39.631
Republican Congressman
Thomas Massie from Kentucky

00:11:39.631 --> 00:11:41.467
tried to question
Kerry's credentials,

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:43.669
specifically his college degree.

00:11:43.669 --> 00:11:45.904
Kerry has a Bachelor of Arts
in Political Science,

00:11:45.904 --> 00:11:47.940
a common degree that
lots of people have.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.909
And yet Massie thought it was
some kind of brilliant "Gotcha!"

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:52.243
to point that out,

00:11:52.243 --> 00:11:54.279
resulting in one of the dumbest
lines of questioning

00:11:54.279 --> 00:11:56.114
in the history of American
politics.

00:11:56.114 --> 00:11:58.617
-It sounds like you're
questioning the credentials

00:11:58.617 --> 00:12:01.153
of the president's advisers
currently.

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:04.323
But I don't think we should
question your credentials today.

00:12:04.323 --> 00:12:08.994
Isn't it true you have
a science degree from Yale?

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:11.396
What's that?
-Bachelor of Arts degree.

00:12:11.396 --> 00:12:13.298
-Is it a political science
degree?

00:12:13.298 --> 00:12:15.066
-Yes, political science.

00:12:15.066 --> 00:12:17.803
-So how do you get a bachelor
of arts in a science?

00:12:17.803 --> 00:12:19.238
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.238 --> 00:12:22.141
-Well, it's a liberal arts
education and degree.

00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:23.375
It's a bachelor.

00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:25.077
-Okay,
so it's not really science.

00:12:25.077 --> 00:12:27.379
So I think it's somewhat
appropriate that somebody

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:31.317
with a pseudoscience degree
is here pushing pseudoscience

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:33.219
in front of our committee today.

00:12:33.219 --> 00:12:34.619
-[ Scoffs ]

00:12:34.619 --> 00:12:37.122
I want to ask you --
-Are you serious?

00:12:37.122 --> 00:12:39.791
I mean, this is really
a serious happening here?

00:12:39.791 --> 00:12:42.394
-Yeah. It is.

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:44.363
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:48.901
Unfortunately...

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:51.536
I'm sorry to say it is
a serious happening.

00:12:51.536 --> 00:12:53.572
And that is the perfect
phrasing.

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.807
Because this whole Trump era
feels like a horror movie

00:12:55.807 --> 00:12:57.509
called "A Serious Happening."

00:12:57.509 --> 00:12:58.510
[ Laughter ]

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.346
This is an actual
member of Congress

00:13:00.346 --> 00:13:01.881
who can't wrap his heard
around the fact

00:13:01.881 --> 00:13:03.815
that you can get a bachelor
of arts degree

00:13:03.815 --> 00:13:05.484
in political science,

00:13:05.484 --> 00:13:08.820
despite the fact that he himself
has a degree from MIT!

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.589
I mean, why stop there, Massie?

00:13:10.589 --> 00:13:13.792
[ As Massie ] "Senator Kerry,
you're a married man, correct?

00:13:13.792 --> 00:13:15.594
Then please explain to us

00:13:15.594 --> 00:13:19.465
how you could possibly have
a bachelor's degree."

00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:23.368
[ Laughter ]

00:13:23.368 --> 00:13:26.539
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:30.842 --> 00:13:34.746
[ Normal voice ] Also, not
that anything matters anymore,

00:13:34.746 --> 00:13:38.383
but that's the same John Kerry
who was falsely criticized

00:13:38.383 --> 00:13:40.719
by conservatives
not for avoiding Vietnam,

00:13:40.719 --> 00:13:43.555
but for going and supposedly
doing a bad job.

00:13:43.555 --> 00:13:46.224
Meanwhile these same
conservatives now heap praise

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:47.993
on Lieutenant Bone Spurs
over here,

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:50.963
whose only Purple Heart is
the one struggling to get air

00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:53.465
through his gravy-clogged veins.

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:54.934
Again nothing matters!

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:55.934
Because these are the people

00:13:55.934 --> 00:13:57.269
protecting the president
in Congress.

00:13:57.269 --> 00:13:59.338
The president refuses to release
his tax returns

00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:01.206
and calls anyone who
investigates him treasonous,

00:14:01.206 --> 00:14:03.309
and Republicans actually expect
us to believe

00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:05.644
that they're the party
of the Constitution

00:14:05.644 --> 00:14:06.812
and the rule of law.

00:14:06.812 --> 00:14:08.380
I don't know if anyone
still believes that.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.414
But if they do...

00:14:09.414 --> 00:14:12.117
-It must really suck
to be that dumb.

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:13.352
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:13.352 --> 00:14:15.087
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:15.087 --> 00:14:16.889 line:0%
♪♪

